IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`

-- aia-literacy: Article 4 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): AI literacy.
-- The Omnibus REPLACED Article 4. As enacted it is one paragraph (a duty of providers and deployers "to ensure, to their best extent, a
-- sufficient level of AI literacy"); as amended it has three paragraphs (a duty "to support the development of AI literacy", with the
-- sentence that no specific level of any individual's literacy must be guaranteed; support by the Commission and the Member States; the Board's recommendations).
-- Article 4 is in Chapter I, which applies from 2 February 2025 (Art 113 third paragraph, point (a)). Before that every function answers NOTHING.
-- READ-ONLY for the parts. The meaning of "AI literacy" is Art 3(56) (aia-definitions.l4).

§ `Has Chapter I begun to apply?`

GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 4 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter I` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

§ `Article 4(1): the duty of providers and deployers`

-- src:153 | 1. Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to support the development of AI literacy of their staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on their behalf, taking into account their technical knowledge, experience, education and training and the context the AI systems are to be used in, and considering the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used. This obligation does not require providers or deployers to guarantee any specific level of AI literacy of any individual.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:596 | Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to ensure, to their best extent, a sufficient level of AI literacy of their staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on their behalf, taking into account their technical knowledge, experience, education and training and the context the AI systems are to be used in, and considering the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used.
@ref Art 4(1) (src:153) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:596)
-- Both texts address "Providers and deployers of AI systems".
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party is a provider of an AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party is a deployer of an AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(1) the party owes the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 4 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF `the party is a provider of an AI system` OR `the party is a deployer of an AI system`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures"

-- src:153 | 1. Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to support the development of AI literacy of their staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on their behalf, taking into account their technical knowledge, experience, education and training and the context the AI systems are to be used in, and considering the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used. This obligation does not require providers or deployers to guarantee any specific level of AI literacy of any individual.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:596 | Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to ensure, to their best extent, a sufficient level of AI literacy of their staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on their behalf, taking into account their technical knowledge, experience, education and training and the context the AI systems are to be used in, and considering the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used.
@ref Art 4(1) (src:153) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:596)
-- fork F-4-1: a measure that lacks an element of the duty does not meet it (JUST FALSE). A bare "shall" not done: the text does not say what
-- follows, so the other reading is NOTHING. The judgments ("sufficient", "support the development") are plain inputs.
-- VERSION as enacted: the measures ensure, to the party's best extent, a sufficient level of AI literacy.
-- VERSION as amended: the measures support the development of AI literacy; the party need not guarantee any specific level (next function).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the measures concern the AI literacy of the party's staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measures take into account the technical knowledge, experience, education and training of those persons and the context the AI systems are to be used in` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measures consider the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measures are to ensure, to the party's best extent, a sufficient level of AI literacy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measures are to support the development of AI literacy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(1) the measures meet the duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 4 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE IF       `the measures concern the AI literacy of the party's staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on its behalf`
              AND `the measures take into account the technical knowledge, experience, education and training of those persons and the context the AI systems are to be used in`
              AND `the measures consider the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used`
              AND CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
                  WHEN `as enacted` THEN `the measures are to ensure, to the party's best extent, a sufficient level of AI literacy`   -- VERSION as enacted
                  WHEN `as amended` THEN `the measures are to support the development of AI literacy`                                 -- VERSION as amended
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case; fork F-4-1): "Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to ..."

-- src:153 | 1. Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to support the development of AI literacy of their staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on their behalf, taking into account their technical knowledge, experience, education and training and the context the AI systems are to be used in, and considering the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used. This obligation does not require providers or deployers to guarantee any specific level of AI literacy of any individual.
@ref Art 4(1) (src:153)
-- The sentence "This obligation does not require providers or deployers to guarantee any specific level of AI literacy of any individual" is in the text as amended only.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party is a provider of an AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party is a deployer of an AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(1) the party must guarantee a specific level of AI literacy of an individual` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 4 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence is not in the text as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN          -- VERSION as amended
             IF `the party is a provider of an AI system` OR `the party is a deployer of an AI system`
             THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This obligation does not require providers or deployers to guarantee any specific level of AI literacy of any individual"
             ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks of providers and deployers

-- The regulative rule: a provider and a deployer each owe the measures. The text gives neither a time limit nor a consequence, so no trace can
-- reach BREACH (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path). Before Chapter I applies nothing is owed.
DECLARE `Art 4(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 4(1) take measures regarding AI literacy`

-- src:153 | 1. Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to support the development of AI literacy of their staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on their behalf, taking into account their technical knowledge, experience, education and training and the context the AI systems are to be used in, and considering the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used. This obligation does not require providers or deployers to guarantee any specific level of AI literacy of any individual.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:596 | Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to ensure, to their best extent, a sufficient level of AI literacy of their staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on their behalf, taking into account their technical knowledge, experience, education and training and the context the AI systems are to be used in, and considering the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used.
@ref Art 4(1) (src:153) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:596)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 4(1) act`
`Art 4(1) the provider's duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` MEANS
    IF `Art 4 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 4(1) take measures regarding AI literacy`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before 2 February 2025

-- src:153 | 1. Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to support the development of AI literacy of their staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on their behalf, taking into account their technical knowledge, experience, education and training and the context the AI systems are to be used in, and considering the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used. This obligation does not require providers or deployers to guarantee any specific level of AI literacy of any individual.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:596 | Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to ensure, to their best extent, a sufficient level of AI literacy of their staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on their behalf, taking into account their technical knowledge, experience, education and training and the context the AI systems are to be used in, and considering the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used.
@ref Art 4(1) (src:153) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:596)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 4(1) act`
`Art 4(1) the deployer's duty to take measures regarding AI literacy` MEANS
    IF `Art 4 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         MUST `Art 4(1) take measures regarding AI literacy`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before 2 February 2025

§ `Article 4(2) and (3): support by the Commission and the Member States, and the Board's recommendations (as amended only)`

-- src:154 | 2. The Commission and the Member States shall support and facilitate the efforts of providers and deployers of AI systems, in particular SMEs, in fulfilling their obligation under paragraph 1 of this Article. For that purpose, the Commission shall publish practical examples of how to comply with that obligation on the single information platform referred to in Article 62(3), point (b).
@ref Art 4(2) (src:154)
-- Addressed to officials. What it means to a provider or deployer: it may expect that support. The text names no claim and no remedy.
-- "in particular SMEs" stresses a group of the beneficiaries; it limits nothing.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party is a provider or a deployer of AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(2) the Commission and the Member States must support and facilitate the efforts of the party to fulfil the obligation under paragraph 1` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 4 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph 2 is not in the text as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN          -- VERSION as amended
             IF `the party is a provider or a deployer of AI systems`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the efforts of providers and deployers of AI systems"

-- src:154 | 2. The Commission and the Member States shall support and facilitate the efforts of providers and deployers of AI systems, in particular SMEs, in fulfilling their obligation under paragraph 1 of this Article. For that purpose, the Commission shall publish practical examples of how to comply with that obligation on the single information platform referred to in Article 62(3), point (b).
@ref Art 4(2) second sentence (src:154)
-- "For that purpose, the Commission shall publish practical examples ... on the single information platform referred to in Article 62(3), point (b)."
-- No time limit and no consequence: no breach path.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(2) the Commission must publish practical examples of how to comply with the obligation under paragraph 1` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 4 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph 2 is not in the text as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended

-- src:155 | 3. The Board shall adopt recommendations, taking into account European competence frameworks, to support the Commission and Member States in the promotion of AI literacy required under paragraph 1, including by setting out common objectives.
@ref Art 4(3) (src:155)
-- The Board adopts recommendations "to support the Commission and Member States in the promotion of AI literacy required under paragraph 1". An official's duty
-- with no time limit and no consequence: no breach path.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(3) the Board must adopt recommendations to support the promotion of AI literacy` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 4 Chapter I has begun to apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025" (Art 113(a))
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph 3 is not in the text as enacted
         WHEN `as amended` THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as amended
